{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nAll done. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**Root cause: `_normalize_requested_path` only called `unquote()` once, so double-encoded traversal (`%252e%252e%252f`) bypassed the `\"..\"` check. The absolute-path guard (`startswith(\"/\")`) was dead code because it ran after `lstrip(\"/\")`. The ancestry check used fragile string-prefix matching."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nAll tasks are complete — both the validator and `make test` passed successfully. Here's what was done:\n\n**Bug fix in `repo/export_api/storage.py`:**\n1. **Iterative decoding** — `unquote()` is now called in a loop until stable, catching double/multi-encoded traversal like `%252e%252e%252f`\n2. **Absolute-path guard moved before stripping** — absolute paths (`/etc/passwd`) and drive-letter paths (`C:\\temp\\`) are now blocked in `_normalize_requested_path` before `lstrip(\"/\")`\n3. **Split-based `\"..\"` detection** — uses `normalized.split(\"/\")` instead of substring `\"..\" in normalized` to avoid false positives (e.g., `..hidden`)\n4. **`Path.relative_to()` ancestry check** — replaced the fragile string-prefix check with proper path containment, handling symlinks correctly\n\n**Artifacts created:**\n- `audit/triage_note.json` — triage disposition for all 4 findings (2 fixed, 2 deferred)\n- `repo/ops/deploy_hotfix.json` — deploy note with verification steps and behavior preservation claims for all 6 request samples\n- `repo/tests/test_hotfix_regressions.py` — 4 regression tests covering encoded traversal, double-encoded traversal, nested exports, and all request samples"}}
